method.description:
The layer names [param entity] resolves to on this peer, ordered by name so that two peers that learned the same memberships in different orders read the same list.
Server authority answers the committed row. A peer holding no committed row answers its own declared labels, which is the only interest fact a non-authoritative peer legitimately has.
[codeblock]
for name in core.interest_membership_ids(entity):
    var layer := api.layer_find(name)
[/codeblock]

Whether [param destination], in whatever form it arrived, names the scene declared as [param label].
A destination arrives in whichever form the requester used, so a handler that tests the raw value against one form silently admits or refuses the other. This matches in order: the exact text against [param label], then [param destination] read as a resource path and resolved through its [String] basename, then the path declared for [param label] itself, resolved the same way, against that basename. A [param destination] that is neither a [String] nor a [StringName] targets nothing, and a path that does not resolve under [code]res://[/code] targets nothing. The declared-path step needs the reader [method set_scene_path_reader] installs. With none installed, this answers false rather than guessing.
[codeblock]
api.scene_set_request_handler(
    func(_who, destination, _args) -> Error:
        if api.scene_request_targets(destination, &"Arena"):
            return OK
        return ERR_UNAUTHORIZED,
)
[/codeblock]
